F1: single G state object; makeRng seeded PRNG used everywhere; resolveTurnCore fixed order (hazard→production→needs→fatigue→morale). Score 2.

F2: genMap() 8x8 uses seeded G.rng; canBuildAt checks def.terrain.includes(tile.terrain); adjacency bonus added to base yield in resolveProduction. Score 2.

F3: ore→metal (mine→forge), ash→soil→food (composter→greenhouse); storageCap/addRes cap+log overflow. Score 2.

F4: colonist records {skill,fatigue,morale,job,assigned}; skillFactor/fatigueFactor/moraleFactor read in resolveProduction. Score 2.

F5: resolveNeeds consumes food/water, shortage lowers morale via delta, +2 morale on met needs (recovery). Score 2.

F6: 9 RESEARCH nodes with prereq[]; canResearch enforces; purchaseResearch deducts cost; effects read (stormMitigation, condenserMult, generatorMult, repairDiscount, prereqResearch gates). Score 2.

F7: 12 EVENTS, weight field via pickWeighted; 5 events w/ 2-choice branches (wandererArrives, contaminatedWater, colonistDispute, ashLungSickness, raiderSkirmish); eventState cooldown tracked/checked. Score 2.

F8: buyPrice() uses market.drift (drifts per turn) * stock ratio; market.inventory[].qty limited and decremented; tradeBuy/tradeSell both functional. Score 2.

F9: resolveHazard fires every 8 turns, severity=8+floor(turn/8)*3; damageFactor(b.damage) cuts production; windbreak/stormShelters/reinforced mitigate; repairCost/repairBuilding spend parts, reset damage. Score 2.

F10: serializeState→JSON.stringify into textarea; loadBtn JSON.parse + validateSaveObj with specific error messages. Score 2.

F11: checkEndConditions has win (turn≥60,pop≥12,no shortage) and lose (pop==0), called every finishTurn; computeScore combines pop/research/stock/turn; showEndScreen renders summary. Score 2.

F12: switchTab wired to tab buttons; renderLog shows "T{turn}"; attachTooltip/resTooltipHtml/tileTooltipHtml explain sourced numbers; Space/1-5 keydown handlers; @media(max-width:480px) layout rules. Score 2.

F13: runTests() has ~30 real invariant assertions (cap enforcement, PRNG determinism, id-link consistency, bounds); runBenchmark() runs 200 headless turns via greedyPolicyTurn+endTurnAuto, returns stateHash. Score 2.

G1: efficientCondensers.condenserMult / geothermal.generatorMult read into yieldMult inside resolveProduction, applied every turn to real output. Score 4.

G2: resolveNeeds sets foodShort/waterShort → morale delta on colonists → moraleFactor(c.morale) multiplies production ratio in resolveProduction next resolution. Score 4.

G3: resolveHazard sets b.damage → damageFactor(b.damage) cuts finalRatio in resolveProduction → repairCost(scales w/ damage, reinforced discount)→repairBuilding spends parts, resets damage to 0 restoring output. Score 4.

G4: buyPrice() = TRADE_BASE_PRICE * market.drift[r] (drifts via updateMarketForNewTurn each turn) * scarcity ratio from G.res[res]/cap. Score 4.

G5: wandererArrives choices push new colonist+consume food/water vs add scrip+lower all morale; contaminatedWater choices deduct parts vs lose water%+morale — real state writes, not just logs. Score 4.

